{
 "_id": "JgbhHu3Xdg6y4dKN",
 "name": "Domain Expansion: Idle Death Gamble",
 "type": "spell",
 "img": "modules/jjk5e/icons/techniques/pachinko-fever-domain.svg",
 "system": {
  "description": {
   "value": "<p><em>Pachinko Fever — Innate Technique (3rd level)</em></p><p><em>Domain Expansion (rules): full-turn action, 20 CE unless stated, 175-ft radius, 1 minute. When the domain ends you suffer <strong>Technique Burnout</strong> (applied automatically by the module).</em></p><p>At 3rd level, you gain access to your domain expansion.  Once per long rest you can expand your domain for free bringing you and all creatures of your choice within 175 feet to a demiplane that resembles a subway station as music starts playing. This domain is Non-Lethal with <em>Anti-Domain Clash</em> as listed in Non-Lethal Domains and cannot be reacted to unless the opposing user has a domain with at least 400 refinement points and has higher refinement than you.<br />\n You gain three types of Pachinko attacks that can be used as a bonus action, each attack increases the \"expectation\" by a percentage.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Green Balls.</strong> As a bonus action for 1 cursed energy, make a ranged cursed energy attack roll against a target within 30ft. It deals 1d4 bludgeoning damage on a hit and raises expectations by 10%.  </p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Red Rod.</strong> As a bonus action for 3 cursed energy, make a melee cursed energy attack roll against a target. It deals 1d8 bludgeoning damage on a hit and raises expectations by 25%.  </p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Golden Train Door Attack.</strong> As a bonus action for 4 cursed energy, make a melee or ranged cursed energy attack roll against a target within 30ft. On a hit, the target takes 1d12 bludgeoning damage and must make a Strength saving throw or be restrained until the end of your turn. This attack increases expectations by 50%.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>You can consume the expectation at any time by using your bonus action to place your bet and causing an event to take place.<br />\n There are 4 possible types of events. To know which event will happen, you must roll a d20 + your expectation bonus. You get a +1 bonus for every 10% Expectation, to a maximum of +19 at 190%.</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">Number</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">Event Type</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">Description</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">Jackpot Dice</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">1-9</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">Transport Gate</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">Will they make it in?</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">d12</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">10-14</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">Seat Argument</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">Can she get the seat?</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">d10</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">15-18</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">Tight Squeeze</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">Can they get to the bathroom?</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">d8</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">19-20</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">Last Train</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">Can they catch the train?</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">d6</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Once an event starts, roll a d10 to see how many rounds the event lasts. If your domain ends, you immediately roll.</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Number Rolled</th>\n<th>Multiplier</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>1-12</td>\n<td>3</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>13-15</td>\n<td>4</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>16-17</td>\n<td>5</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>18-19</td>\n<td>10</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>20</td>\n<td>Rainbow</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>At the end of the event, you must roll a d20 (also adding expectation to this roll, +1 per 10%) to find out if you win the multiplier bonus or the rare \"Rainbow\" bonus. You can reroll all jackpot dice an amount of times equal to your multiplier, if \"Rainbow\" lands you have an automatic jackpot in that event. At the end of the event you will roll 3dX, with the value of the dice defined by the event. If 3 of the same numbers land, you win a jackpot. When you hit a jackpot the domain expansion is undone without the effects of <em>Technique Burnout</em>, your cursed energy becomes infinite, and you become immortal.<br />\n You gain the following benefits for 4 Rounds:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Your cursed energy completely refuels at the beginning of your turn.  </p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>You will receive the effects of <em>Reverse Cursed Technique</em> as if you have spent cursed energy up to your Cursed Energy modifier at the beginning of your turns. In addition, you cannot go below 1 hit point and heal all injuries.  </p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>You regain one free use of <em>Idle Death Gamble</em>.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>After spending all of your uses, you can use your domain again for 20 Cursed Energy.  </p>",
   "chat": ""
  },
